# Astral Visionary — one of the five Guildlords of the 1997 game, the deck as the original shipped it.
# tier: 11/12 The Guildlords — 35 to 45 life, can't be bribed
# enemy: Astral Visionary (1997 in-game name, s30/assets/text/Advstrings.txt @CREATURENAMES)
# designer: Coyote Tex, MicroProse designer/producer — every enemy deck (precon page, ref. 2)
# variant: Original (base game; the enemy deck files are dated 19 September 1996)
# source: ../shandalar-src/Decks.zip:Decks/0245.dck "Astral Visionary (Ub)" [Tier 3 — Manalink 3
#   file dated 2016-02-15; its first 15 maindeck lines are the 1997 deck, the 16 lines (59
#   cards) after them are the modern deck Manalink appended and are NOT shipped; its
#   .vNone/.v<Colour> sections are the 1997 colour-keyed swaps]
# source: ../s30/assets/configs/rogues/astral_visionary.toml (main_cards, sideboard_cards, level
#   11) [Tier 3 — equals the 1997 prefix above]
# source: ../mage-go/rogue_dck/astral_visionary.dck [Tier 3 — equals the 1997 prefix]
# cross-check: https://mtg.wiki/page/Shandalar_Enemy_Decks_(Guildlords) — "Astral Visionary"
#   (Original) [Tier-web — maindeck agrees]
# group: 1997 originals
name: Astral Visionary
24 Island
4 Counterspell
1 Ancestral Recall
1 Time Walk
1 Timetwister
1 Copy Artifact
4 Leviathan
4 Stasis
1 Mox Sapphire
1 Black Lotus
2 Twiddle
4 Yotian Soldier
4 Howling Mine
4 Zephyr Falcon
3 Unstable Mutation
3 Drain Power
# The 1997 file's colour-keyed sideboard sections. The AI played the maindeck WITHOUT
# .vNone plus the one section matching the player's deck colour (.vNone by default);
# .vNone is folded into the maindeck above, and SB: holds, per name, the largest
# colour-section count minus the .vNone count — the smallest sideboard from which
# every 1997 configuration can be rebuilt by swapping.
#   .vNone   3 Drain Power
#   .vBlack  3 Drain Power
#   .vBlue   3 Drain Power
#   .vGreen  2 Lifetap, 1 Drain Power
#   .vRed    2 Blue Elemental Blast, 1 Drain Power
#   .vWhite  3 Drain Power
SB: 2 Lifetap
SB: 2 Blue Elemental Blast
